  "review": "Independent reviewer executed exact-source heldout1, separate actualTLS negative controls2, nonTLS options3/cache controls2; final code reviewed by coordinator. No original production cleanup defect established.",
  "limitations": [
    "One stable application-read boundary and two handled Node signals only; SIGKILL/crash/power-loss and other interruption points remain unaccepted.",
    "No graceful TLS close_notify or complete memory zeroization proof for interrupted cases.",
    "Port refusal/rebind is endpoint observation, not proof of all kernel TCP states. Child/launcher exit and owned-root removal are checked separately before helper fallback cleanup.",
    "Only successful held-out runtime identity is retained individually; aggregate signal cases verify the same pinned build contract but do not retain separate per-case artifact identities.",
    "Private negative sensitivity controls deliberately alter test instrumentation; they are not original production defects.",
    "Peer/read KeyUpdate, WRITE retry completion, overlapping obligations, control/alert/shutdown and sequence/key usage admission remain pending.",
    "No complete TLS-state inventory, semantic exporter/importer, distinct TLS-code version change, native NGINX integration, performance/security/novelty/10x acceptance."
  ]
